From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:43:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the CPU speed bin cell to
 the SID

The CPU operating points depend on the speed bin that bits 15:8 of the
DVFS fuse word at 0x4c of the SID hold.

Add that word as an nvmem cell. It lies inside the thermal sensor
calibration cell at 0x44, which spans 12 bytes: bits 7:0 of the word
belong to the calibration data of sensor 4, and bits 15:8 are
the speed bin. The nvmem core does not reject overlapping cells.

Not covered: the operating points that use the cell.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the cell reads as the
speed bin of the die, bin 4 on one board and bin 5 on the other, and the
driver gets the bin through it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index c1957cc85852..5052e2369eb8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -694,6 +694,10 @@ sid: efuse@3006000 {
 			ths_calibration: thermal-sensor-calibration@44 {
 				reg = <0x44 0xc>;
 			};
+
+			cpu_speed_grade: cpu-speed-grade@4c {
+				reg = <0x4c 0x4>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		gic: interrupt-controller@3400000 {
